      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{68098a4626271974ef4d2775|full_name}  The issue you have mentioned as \"Duplicated of\" seems related to links on the websites.\n\nBut this one is related to Portals in game.\n\nBefore the new UI update, when you were about to drop a Group+ there was a button with a lock on it that would decide the visibility of the portal for people not part of the group (picture 1 from a VRChat update thumbnail, that lock was available also for Group+).\n\nWhen the lock on the icon was opened, your portal would be visible to people not part of the group, if locked only people from the group would be able to see it.\n\nWith the new ingame UI this functionality looks like is not exposed anymore for Group+ (picture 2 and 3), but is still present when you create Friend+ portals (picture 4 and 5) and is accessible through a check box by the name \"Only Friends can enter portal\".\n\nThis feature was working yesterday, since with our group we use it extensively, but from today's build this functionality is nowhere to be found.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2026-11-25T14:57:17.744Z",
  "deleteID": null,
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Description\n\nWith the new UI is not possible to create Group+ unlocked portals. The feature was present before the new UI and its removal was not mentioned in any changelog so I guess is an unwanted behavior.\n\nThe lack of the feature make it hard for some community I'm a moderator for to properly conduct their events.\n\nReproduction Steps\n\n1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Get into any public instance\n\n3. Drop a Group+ portal\n\n4. Anybody not in your friend list or not in the group will not see the portal.\n\nNo workarounds found, unless you open a Group Public wich is something we don't want to do.\n\nWith the old UI the feature was present and everybody was able to see the Group+ portal.\n\nDetails\n\n- Category: User Interface\n\n- Frequency: Always\n\n---\n\nplatform: PC (platform: Windows, store: Steam, headset: None)\n\nrawPlatform: WindowsPlayer\n\nclientVersion: 2026.4.2-1953-d52354d5be-Release\n\nunityVersion: 6000.0.67f1-DWR\n\nIn-Client Report\n\n---\n\n**Log file:** [output_log_2026-11-25_15-26-24.txt](https://api.vrchat.cloud/api/1/file/file_49b94987-ead4-4cce-b7b1-56d16d7a89fb/1/file)",
